      "term": "Paneer",
      "definition": "A fresh acid-set cheese from South Asia, made by curdling warm milk with lemon juice or vinegar. Unlike most cheeses, paneer does not melt when heated, which makes it ideal for curries where the cheese needs to hold its shape."
